adjudication.rationale:
In packages/core/EventManager.ts inside createAllCalendarEvents, the new loop over destination calendars has an else branch for destinations without credentialId:

```ts
const destinationCalendarCredentials = this.calendarCredentials.filter((c) => c.type === destination.integration);
createdEvents = createdEvents.concat(
  await Promise.all(destinationCalendarCredentials.map(async (c) => await createEvent(c, event)))
);
```

But packages/core/CalendarManager.ts changed createEvent to accept an optional `externalId?: string` and now returns it as `externalId` on the EventResult. EventManager later persists `externalCalendarId` from `result.externalId` (not from `evt.destinationCalendar`). Since this branch does not pass `destination.externalId` into `createEvent`, `result.externalId` will be `undefined`, so the stored `externalCalendarId` will be missing for events created via this path (a regression compared to the previous behavior where it could be derived from destinationCalendar).

In packages/core/EventManager.ts the new logic treats destinationCalendar as an array:

```ts
const [mainHostDestinationCalendar] = evt.destinationCalendar ?? [];
if (evt.location === MeetLocationType && mainHostDestinationCalendar.integration !== "google_calendar") {
  ...
}
```

If `evt.destinationCalendar` is `undefined`, `null`, or an empty array (which the diff explicitly introduces in multiple places, e.g. bookingReminder sets `destinationCalendar: []` when none), then `mainHostDestinationCalendar` is `undefined`. Accessing `mainHostDestinationCalendar.integration` will throw a `TypeError`.

This makes Meet-location events without a destination calendar crash at runtime, so the finding describes a real defect introduced by the diff.

The diff changes `destinationCalendar` to an array and then in `packages/core/EventManager.ts` does:
```ts
const [mainHostDestinationCalendar] = evt.destinationCalendar ?? [];
if (evt.location === MeetLocationType && mainHostDestinationCalendar.integration !== "google_calendar")
```
If `evt.destinationCalendar` is `null`, `undefined`, or `[]`, `mainHostDestinationCalendar` is `undefined` and the unguarded `.integration` access will throw before any calendar work runs. The same diff introduces callers that explicitly set `destinationCalendar: []` (e.g. `bookingReminder.ts`, updated e2e expecting `[]`), making this crash path reachable. The finding’s core claim (unguarded dereference when `null` becomes `[]`) is therefore verifiable in the diff.
